<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105406" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐχ-ίᾱσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a disease of the eyelids, when they are introverted, and
				the lashes irritate the eye</i> (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτρόπιον</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.437
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sever.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				7.68
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a disease of the urethra, when the urine is full of small
				hair-like substances,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(2).768
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>a disease in the breasls of women giving suck, such that the
				nipples crack into fine fissures,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>a fissure, scratch</i> in a bone, <i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i><i>in Hp.Fract.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				12.273
			</span></i> C., [<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				14.782
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>